# What must NOT be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# The build context is `bookstore-platform/` for every service, and it is copied over a socket before
# the first instruction runs. Without this file that copy includes every module's `target/` — nine
# builds' worth of jars and class files, several hundred megabytes — none of which the build stage
# uses, because the build stage compiles from source inside the image.
#
# The second, quieter reason: a file that reaches the context can be COPYed in by accident. A stale
# `target/classes/application-dev.yml` baked into an image would be the Step 6d ghost-file bug again,
# except this time immutable and shipped.

target/
*/target/
.git
.gitignore
.idea
*.iml

# Not source. The Lambda has no image (it is deployed as a jar), and the AWS scripts run from a laptop.
cover.png
test-platform.http
README.md
